# $name

$description

* **Owner:** $owner
* **Pattern:** transactional (queue-based) - the AutoStation equivalent of the UiPath REFramework
* **Data classification:** $classification

## How it maps to the REFramework

| REFramework | This payload |
|---|---|
| Init All Settings (Config.xlsx) | `init()` - manifest `assets` + slot `params` |
| Dispatcher (Add Queue Item) | `dispatch(q, cfg)` - `q.add(reference, payload)`; duplicate references are ignored |
| Get Transaction Data | `q.next()` |
| Process (business logic) | `process_transaction(item)` |
| Business Rule Exception (no retry) | `raise wrapper.DataError(...)` -> `q.fail_business` |
| System Exception (retry) | transient faults retried by `wrapper.run_with_retry`, then `q.fail_system(max_retries)` re-queues |
| Action Center / validation station | `raise NeedsReview(reason)` -> `q.needs_review` (shows on the dashboard) |
| MaxConsecutiveSystemExceptions | `max_consecutive_system_exceptions` param |
| End Process | `wrapper.set_result(...)` summary |

Slots in `manifest-entry.yaml`: a daily `dispatch` slot and an hourly `perform` slot (`mode` param). Use `mode=both` for small jobs.

## Develop

```bash
python -m wrapper_core dev . --param mode=both       # real lifecycle, offline
python -m wrapper_core assist review main.py         # compliance review
python -m pytest
```

Replace `fetch_source_items()` and `process_transaction()`; everything else is the framework. Queue API:
`wrapper_core.activities.queue` (`open`, `add`, `next`, `succeed`, `fail_business`, `fail_system`, `needs_review`, `counts`) - see `docs/ACTIVITIES.md`.
